1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,442
A mango drops from a branch.

2
00:00:02,442 --> 00:00:04,286
A coin slips off a table.

3
00:00:04,286 --> 00:00:05,822
A drop leaves a tap.

4
00:00:06,222 --> 00:00:09,083
Three different things, one
same pull from the Earth.

5
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:13,203
Diya sees a mango fall from
the tree outside her window.

6
00:00:13,203 --> 00:00:16,715
From four point nine metres,
it lands in one second.

7
00:00:17,065 --> 00:00:21,248
Her puzzle: if the branch were twice
as high, would the mango take two

8
00:00:21,248 --> 00:00:22,148
seconds?

9
00:00:22,395 --> 00:00:23,771
Most people say yes.

10
00:00:23,771 --> 00:00:26,828
By the end, you will see
why the answer is no.

11
00:00:27,479 --> 00:00:29,723
So what is motion under gravity?

12
00:00:29,723 --> 00:00:34,170
When only gravity acts on a falling
object, we call it free fall.

13
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:35,582
We ignore the air.

14
00:00:35,982 --> 00:00:41,147
In free fall, every object speeds up at
the same rate, called g, the acceleration

15
00:00:41,147 --> 00:00:42,297
due to gravity.

16
00:00:42,697 --> 00:00:47,259
Near the Earth's surface, g is about
nine point eight metres per second,

17
00:00:47,259 --> 00:00:48,275
every second.

18
00:00:48,275 --> 00:00:49,859
It always points down.

19
00:00:50,459 --> 00:00:54,255
Heavy or light, without air they
all gain speed at the same rate.

20
00:00:54,905 --> 00:00:56,863
Let's drop a mango from rest.

21
00:00:57,213 --> 00:01:01,101
After one second, it moves at nine
point eight metres per second.

22
00:01:01,501 --> 00:01:03,997
After two seconds, nineteen point six.

23
00:01:03,997 --> 00:01:06,838
After three seconds,
twenty nine point four.

24
00:01:07,238 --> 00:01:10,717
Every second, the speed grows
by the same nine point eight.

25
00:01:10,717 --> 00:01:12,711
So the graph is a straight line.

26
00:01:13,211 --> 00:01:14,651
Slow-motion replay.

27
00:01:14,651 --> 00:01:16,396
Freeze at one second.

28
00:01:16,796 --> 00:01:18,401
The red arrow is g.

29
00:01:18,401 --> 00:01:19,771
It never changes.

30
00:01:19,771 --> 00:01:22,082
The blue arrow is the velocity.

31
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,452
It keeps growing.

32
00:01:23,952 --> 00:01:25,471
Now the ghost copies.

33
00:01:25,471 --> 00:01:27,345
The gaps grow every second.

34
00:01:27,745 --> 00:01:30,250
First second, four point nine metres.

35
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:32,549
Next second, fourteen point seven.

36
00:01:32,549 --> 00:01:34,457
Then twenty four point five.

37
00:01:34,457 --> 00:01:36,717
In the ratio one, three, five.

38
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:39,568
Now the formulas, step by step.

39
00:01:39,918 --> 00:01:40,818
Step one.

40
00:01:40,763 --> 00:01:42,823
Take the equations of motion.

41
00:01:42,823 --> 00:01:47,079
The mango starts from rest,
so u is zero, and a becomes g.

42
00:01:47,829 --> 00:01:48,729
Step two.

43
00:01:48,711 --> 00:01:51,895
v equals u plus a t becomes v equals g t.

44
00:01:51,895 --> 00:01:54,444
The speed grows in step with time.

45
00:01:55,194 --> 00:01:56,200
Step three.

46
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:01,294
s equals u t plus half a t squared
becomes h equals half g t squared.

47
00:02:01,294 --> 00:02:03,590
Height grows with time squared.

48
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:05,240
Step four.

49
00:02:05,173 --> 00:02:06,953
v squared equals two g h.

50
00:02:06,953 --> 00:02:09,757
It gives the landing
speed without the time.

51
00:02:10,507 --> 00:02:11,620
Remember this.

52
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:15,728
In free fall, the acceleration
is always g, pointing down.

53
00:02:15,728 --> 00:02:16,841
Speed changes.

54
00:02:16,841 --> 00:02:17,861
g does not.

55
00:02:18,561 --> 00:02:19,667
Side by side.

56
00:02:19,667 --> 00:02:24,307
A one kilogram stone and a five
kilogram stone, dropped together with no

57
00:02:24,307 --> 00:02:25,207
air.

58
00:02:25,229 --> 00:02:29,789
The heavy one is pulled five times
harder, but it is also five times harder

59
00:02:29,789 --> 00:02:30,767
to speed up.

60
00:02:31,367 --> 00:02:32,467
Now you try.

61
00:02:32,467 --> 00:02:34,270
Which stone lands first?

62
00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:35,636
Pause and decide.

63
00:02:38,836 --> 00:02:39,736
Together!

64
00:02:39,549 --> 00:02:43,765
The bigger pull and the bigger mass
cancel, so both fall with the same

65
00:02:43,765 --> 00:02:44,665
g.

66
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,985
Watch them fall.

67
00:02:45,985 --> 00:02:47,971
Both land at the same moment.

68
00:02:48,471 --> 00:02:52,746
Now throw a ball straight up at
nineteen point six metres per second.

69
00:02:53,096 --> 00:02:54,547
Take up as positive.

70
00:02:54,547 --> 00:02:58,004
Gravity points down, so a
is minus nine point eight.

71
00:02:58,404 --> 00:03:02,061
Each second it loses nine
point eight metres per second.

72
00:03:02,061 --> 00:03:04,576
After two seconds, velocity is zero.

73
00:03:04,576 --> 00:03:05,868
That is the top.

74
00:03:06,268 --> 00:03:08,757
It has risen nineteen point six metres.

75
00:03:08,757 --> 00:03:11,503
Two seconds later it is back in your hand.

76
00:03:11,903 --> 00:03:13,667
Time up equals time down.

77
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:16,989
It returns with the same
speed, now pointing down.

78
00:03:17,589 --> 00:03:21,943
On the graph, one straight line
slopes down, crossing zero at the top.

79
00:03:22,443 --> 00:03:23,361
Your turn.

80
00:03:23,361 --> 00:03:26,242
At the very top, the velocity is zero.

81
00:03:26,242 --> 00:03:28,353
Is the acceleration zero too?

82
00:03:28,353 --> 00:03:29,704
Pause and decide.

83
00:03:32,904 --> 00:03:33,804
No!

84
00:03:33,325 --> 00:03:35,298
It is still g, pointing down.

85
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:38,358
If it were zero, the ball
would just hang there.

86
00:03:39,008 --> 00:03:40,474
Back to Diya's mango.

87
00:03:40,474 --> 00:03:43,759
From four point nine
metres, it takes one second.

88
00:03:43,759 --> 00:03:46,287
How long from nine point eight metres?

89
00:03:46,787 --> 00:03:49,303
Use h equals half g t squared.

90
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:52,910
So t equals the square
root of two h over g.

91
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:57,217
Two times nine point eight,
over nine point eight, is two.

92
00:03:57,217 --> 00:03:59,239
So t is the square root of two.

93
00:03:59,989 --> 00:04:03,311
That is about one point
four one seconds, not two.

94
00:04:03,311 --> 00:04:07,076
Double the height, and the
time grows only root two times.

95
00:04:07,726 --> 00:04:09,192
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:09,542 --> 00:04:14,209
For a ball thrown up, many students
take up as positive, yet write a equals

97
00:04:14,209 --> 00:04:15,724
plus nine point eight.

98
00:04:16,074 --> 00:04:16,974
Wrong.

99
00:04:16,682 --> 00:04:19,344
Pick one positive direction and keep it.

100
00:04:19,344 --> 00:04:23,771
If up is positive, a is minus g,
both going up and coming down.

101
00:04:24,421 --> 00:04:25,958
Where is this asked?

102
00:04:25,958 --> 00:04:29,558
As numericals on stones
dropped or thrown from towers.

103
00:04:30,158 --> 00:04:31,327
Exam level now.

104
00:04:31,327 --> 00:04:35,723
A ball is thrown straight up at
fifteen metres per second from a twenty

105
00:04:35,723 --> 00:04:36,684
metre tower.

106
00:04:36,684 --> 00:04:37,862
Take g as ten.

107
00:04:37,862 --> 00:04:39,852
When does it hit the ground?

108
00:04:39,852 --> 00:04:41,070
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:47,957
The answer is D.

110
00:04:47,957 --> 00:04:49,132
Four seconds.

111
00:04:49,632 --> 00:04:50,845
Up is positive.

112
00:04:50,845 --> 00:04:54,760
The ground is twenty metres
below, so s is minus twenty.

113
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:59,137
Minus twenty equals fifteen
t minus five t squared.

114
00:04:59,137 --> 00:05:02,793
So t squared minus three
t minus four is zero.

115
00:05:03,293 --> 00:05:05,375
So t is four, or minus one.

116
00:05:05,375 --> 00:05:07,034
Time cannot be negative.

117
00:05:07,034 --> 00:05:10,991
Three seconds is only the trip
back to the top of the tower.

118
00:05:11,591 --> 00:05:13,050
Here is your recap.

119
00:05:13,050 --> 00:05:14,549
Screenshot this card.

120
00:05:17,749 --> 00:05:20,586
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

121
00:05:20,986 --> 00:05:21,886
One.

122
00:05:21,476 --> 00:05:25,103
Why does a heavy stone not
fall faster than a light one?

123
00:05:26,003 --> 00:05:26,903
Two.

124
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:30,158
What is the acceleration of a
ball at the top of its flight?

125
00:05:31,058 --> 00:05:31,958
Three.

126
00:05:31,626 --> 00:05:35,749
If the height becomes four times
bigger, how much longer does the fall

127
00:05:35,749 --> 00:05:36,649
take?

128
00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:40,779
Next time: the mango's fall
draws a curve on a graph.

129
00:05:40,779 --> 00:05:42,724
What does its shape tell you?

130
00:05:42,724 --> 00:05:44,952
We find out in position-time graphs.
